    <briefdescription>
<para>POSIX device I/O control (&lt;<ref refid="ioctl_8h" kindref="compound">sys/ioctl.h</ref>&gt;) </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides <ref refid="group__posix__option__group__xsi__streams_1ga1487536105f7a596481bf6bfa8de99f6" kindref="member">ioctl()</ref> for performing device-specific control operations on file descriptors, along with the standard non-blocking and pending-read flags.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para><ref refid="ioctl_8h" kindref="compound">sys/ioctl.h</ref> is not part of the strict POSIX.1-2017 standard but is a widely-supported extension available on Linux and BSD systems. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
